# Production connection. Copy this file to packages/db/.env.neon and paste the
# string from Neon into it.
#
# Deliberately not named .env — that one points at the local container and is
# loaded automatically by every `pnpm db:*` command. This file is read by
# exactly two commands and nothing else:
#
#   pnpm db:prod:status    # which migrations the deployed database is missing
#   pnpm db:prod:deploy    # apply them
#
# Both print the host they are about to touch before they touch it. Nothing else
# in the repo can reach production, and the destructive scripts (db:migrate,
# db:seed, db:reset) refuse outright to run against a non-local host, so a
# schema change lands there because someone meant it to.
#
# Git-ignored. Never commit the filled-in version.

# The DIRECT (unpooled) string from Neon → Connect → Connection pooling OFF.
# The host has no "-pooler" in it. Migrations need this one: the pooler runs
# PgBouncer in transaction mode, which cannot hold the session-level advisory
# locks the schema engine takes out.
#
# Paste it between the quotes below, replacing PASTE_HERE. Keep the quotes —
# they are what stops the shell from choking on the "&" in the string.
DIRECT_URL="PASTE_HERE"

# The pooled "-pooler" string is not needed here. Only the deployed function
# connects through it, and Vercel supplies it there as DATABASE_URL — set on the
# api project alone. Nothing on a developer's machine should hold it.
